<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bidache</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bidache is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basses-pyrenees">Pyrénées-Atlantiques</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidouze">Bidouze</a> river. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gramont">Gramont family</a>, whose castle dominated the village, and from the 16th century they claimed it as a sovereign principality on the border of France and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. Annexed to France in the Revolution, the castle was burned in 1796 and stands in ruins.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bidache.jpg" alt="Bidache" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bidache.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
